                                                                            
  ### 🛠️ What Was Upgraded                                                   
                                                                             
  1. Enhanced Firestore Security Rules (firestore.rules)                     
      • We updated firestore.rules to fully incorporate the detailed, OWASP- 
      aligned rules from firestore-security.rules.
      • Includes robust checks for access control (A01), injection protection
      (A03), data integrity checks (A08) for prices and quantities, and      
      account status/lockout validations.
  2. Clean Storage Rules Separation (storage.rules)
      • We separated the Storage rules into a dedicated file: storage.rules. 
      • This prevents syntax errors that would occur when trying to deploy   
      Firestore-wrapped rules to the Storage service bucket.
  3. Realtime Database Rules Configuration (database.rules.json)
      • We created database.rules.json to secure the Realtime Database       
      against unauthorized public writes and reads (requiring authentication).
      • Updated firebase.json to reference these rules and added the database
      emulator under the port 9000.
  4. Developer Gateway Configuration (.env.local)
      • Populated the EXPO_PUBLIC_DEVELOPER_EMAIL variable with the developer
      email (boatengadams4g@gmail.com) in .env.local to align with the access
      controls set up in the security rules.
  

